Z||000023||EdsB52||08-12-2001||03:02 PM||||I tried to get on there and refine the page, copy the address and transpose it to the screen, but it still gave the same page address. So try this, hit the site I gave you, go to the left column, and find this bold heading:<P>"Search Engines and Databases"<P>Then go 5 prompts down and hit the "Social Security Death Index"<P>When it pops up type in a full first and last name. Like I said, some names are entered with only the first letter of the first name. Between the name blocks is the soundex if you don't have an accurate spelling of the names. Try not to use that though, just leave it alone. Practice with the names I gave you, type in deceased family members or friends to get the hang and proceed on with your search. These 'find people' sites simply use these public access sites and charge you $40, it's a joke. Good luck.<p>[This message has been edited by EdsB52 (edited 08-12-2001).]||||reg||1
